cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Nemesis Forge: an LLM fleet proposes, deterministic oracles prove"
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite it using the metadata
  below. If you use it to produce a finding, the engine's own reporting
  convention applies: state the rung the evidence reached, and state what was
  not established.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Obi Ebuka
    family-names: David
    alias: "Obi Ebuka David"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, University of Dayton"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eobi/nemesisforge"
abstract: >-
  An autonomous vulnerability discovery engine built around a single
  architectural constraint: a model may propose a candidate at any rung of an
  exploitability ladder, and may certify none of them. Certification comes from
  eight deterministic oracles that are independent of the proposer and
  reproducible by a third party. The engine reports findings at the rung the
  evidence reaches and states, on every finding, what it did not establish.
keywords:
  - vulnerability-discovery
  - fuzzing
  - memory-safety
  - exploitability-triage
  - differential-oracle
  - coordinated-disclosure
  - large-language-models
  - software-security
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-24"
